{"version":"1","id":"hiredscore","handle":"hiredscore","name":"HiredScore Engineering","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/17bfcaa9532e480e86bd1e15f6935918","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":0.5318,"y":-0.81,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":12,"newest_post_at":"2023-12-12T15:12:10.974Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-07-30T06:57:23.759Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":5.5,"summary_length_avg":333.75,"title_length_avg":49.75,"title_length_var":229.020833,"tag_entropy":2.948784,"tag_diversity":1.75,"top_tag_share":0.083333,"avg_upvotes":1.083333,"median_upvotes":0.5,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.071429,"zero_engagement_share":0.5,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.107104,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.2},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-3.2059,-8.6618],"cadence_depth":[-9.5,-0.9706],"hype_variety":[-7.4706,-2.7794],"title_style":[-7.4118,-5.9559]},"top_tags":[["aws",3],["kubernetes",3],["devops",2],["prometheus",2],["testing",2],["infrastructure",2],["argocd",1],["aws-iam",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["The retrospective is the most important part of the sprint","Thanos: Highly Available Prometheus Kubernetes Clusters","Fixing Overlapped Blocks in Thanos"],"outlier":["The Confusing Matrix"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"lE0YO3JnK","title":"Fixing Overlapped Blocks in Thanos","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/fixing-overlaps-in-thanos-ed03c26ed1ed?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/fixing-overlapped-blocks-in-thanos-le0yo3jnk","summary":"Learn how to fix overlapped blocks in Thanos by finding their source and deleting them, thereby restoring compaction and retention. Overlapped blocks can cause issues in Thanos setups, but this post provides a helpful solution.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7f523f6ccbcaa1be477c778adacdb93c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-12T15:12:10.974Z"},{"id":"1SQpqjs95","title":"Written communication \u2014 collaborate with kindness","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/written-communication-collaborate-with-kindness-e7e8c2e2f1b2?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/written-communication-collaborate-with-kindness-1sqpqjs95","summary":"Written communication - collaborate with kindness.com Text messaging has become the go-to communication method. Sasha Ben David: We often rely on facial expressions and tone of voice to pick up on emotional cues. By text you can\u2019t see if a person is confused, finds someting funny or think you were harsh.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/76cd95d83329bd7395bb16416494cec4?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-21T06:43:40.338Z"},{"id":"CJ8cG3oqJ","title":"Manage Kubernetes Secrets with Crossplane and External Secrets","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/manage-kubernetes-secrets-with-crossplane-and-external-secrets-1423302c92fd?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/manage-kubernetes-secrets-with-crossplane-and-external-secrets-cj8cg3oqj","summary":"Manage Kubernetes Secrets with Crossplane and External Secrets with Argo CD, Crossplane, External Secrets Operator. The principles presented here can be easily applied on any major cloud provider and for any resources provided by it. For the demo we\u2019ll skip the ArgoCD part in favor of a simple and mostly skip how the mentioned components need to be deployed securely.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d40b0aaf088ac209e292a49f67805555?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-25T08:29:45.036Z"},{"id":"mYTQhwkNh","title":"Why Do QA Engineers Love Finding Bugs but I Personally Hate It","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/why-do-qa-engineers-love-finding-bugs-but-i-personally-hate-it-4aa59b7e025f?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-do-qa-engineers-love-finding-bugs-but-i-personally-hate-it-mytqhwknh","summary":"Why Do QA Engineers Love Finding Bugs but I Personally Hate It? Shahar Barak: I hate it when we find bugs. When we find a bug, we think: Where did we go wrong? What do we need to do for automated tests? It\u2019s still not perfect at the beginning, but we knew there would be a reduction in quality.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/60dce43c495bf7026f1e18447e0784ed?_a=AQADKfR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-13T12:54:44.832Z"},{"id":"TOBuIBnQf","title":"My framework for defining goals that actually help people grow","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/my-framework-for-defining-goals-that-actually-help-people-grow-34bb41427f1b?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/my-framework-for-defining-goals-that-actually-help-people-grow-tobuibnqf","summary":"Dennis Nerush's framework for defining goals that actually help people grow is hard. He says goals are not measurable and don\u2019t reflect the actual expectations of the manager from the employee. The goals definition should be personal and target the employee\u2019s personal strengths and weaknesses regardless of the \u2018level\u2019 they are at.","image":"https://miro.medium.com/v2/da:true/resize:fit:500/1*JuOsQfXeY6JOLy_XAohy1A.gif","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-03T06:08:30.228Z"},{"id":"sRxpQ7kZb","title":"Every time you don\u2019t clean your code, a debugger whispers \u2018why?\u2019 in despair","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/every-time-you-dont-clean-your-code-a-debugger-whispers-why-in-despair-53b44e908026?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/every-time-you-don-t-clean-your-code-a-debugger-whispers-why-in-despair-srxpq7kzb","summary":"Clean code is a form of art, and nothing less, says author Robert C. Martin. Clean code can be read, and enhanced by a developer other than its original author. The goal of clean code is to reduce the cost of change over time. Clean code is also about making code easier to write as it is to read.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b625b435fb96d2f50154266e0de18d1b","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-02T12:08:05.852Z"},{"id":"bZAOSCn59","title":"The retrospective is the most important part of the sprint","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/the-retrospective-is-the-most-important-part-of-the-sprint-b6463a25cfed?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-retrospective-is-the-most-important-part-of-the-sprint-bzaoscn59","summary":"Retro is an agile ceremony that takes place at the end of every sprint. A couple of months ago we had a re-org in our company, which led to a lot - glad \u2014 was there some good actions taken or feature added or technique learned that we want to share with the rest of the team/group/company?","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/91d4cd99b39db4b93e566f652dcba591","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-11-07T12:55:53.853Z"},{"id":"7JCsibp-f","title":"End To End Deployment with Terraform and Ansible","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/e2e-deployment-with-terraform-and-ansible-8992494ebf79?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/end-to-end-deployment-with-terraform-and-ansible-7jcsibp-f","summary":"Terraform and Ansible are two widely adopted tools used to manage and maintain your infrastructure. The organization uses Ansible as the main configuration management tool. Terraform triggers Ansible with the given SSH key and runs the configuration playbook. The Ansible playbook runs with a local-exec provisioner.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/addf88a3b1c86fc1c9c02ffef82fb1c4","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-08-10T14:14:09.986Z"},{"id":"nFpT1htX4","title":"Thanos: Highly Available Prometheus Kubernetes Clusters","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/using-thanos-to-store-prometheus-on-many-kubernetes-clusters-fd24b63873d8?source=rss----1ecd1a72f23b---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/thanos-highly-available-prometheus-kubernetes-clusters-nfpt1htx4","summary":"In a world where thousands of services and applications are deployed in multiple infrastructures, monitoring in highly-available environments has become an essential part of every development process. HiredScore wanted to create a better high available resilient infrastructure with data retention that would be feasible and cost-efficient. We chose to implement the Kube-Prometheus solution by Bitnami & Thanos by Thanos-io. It seamlessly extends Prometheus in a few simple steps.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/0b30d7982cc3fcf4ccd4af018bb41ed4","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-17T13:34:02.715Z"},{"id":"bIj6aSlLF","title":"Defining Team Vision and Values","url":"https://medium.com/hiredscore-engineering/defining-team-vision-and-values-f71e4d1b77ac","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/defining-team-vision-and-values-bij6asllf","summary":"Every team has a culture, values, and purpose. It doesn\u2019t have to be written in order to exist. Writing them down creates an advantage to such teams as it aligns everyone on the expected behaviors and the purpose of that team. It guides them through difficult decisions and motivates them to achieve that vision of themselves.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b3ed07c847ad16156859d848df0f24b1","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022